These five header files declare NVIDIA's Video Codec SDK interfaces
(NVDEC through libnvcuvid, NVENC through libnvidia-encode, and the parts
of CUDA they need).

Origin : https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers  tag n12.1.14.0
         (NVIDIA's own SDK headers, repackaged so that the driver's
         libraries can be opened at run time instead of linked)
API    : Video Codec SDK 12.1. Needs NVIDIA driver 530.41.03 or newer on
         Linux.
Licence: MIT. The full text is at the top of each file.
Changes: none. The files are as published.

No FFmpeg code is involved: the project that publishes them is run by
FFmpeg developers, but the files contain declarations and a small loader
only.

To move to a newer SDK, replace the five files with those of a newer tag
and check the driver version it asks for.
